# Allows sun.misc.Unsafe memory access, which silences this warning:
#     WARNING: A terminally deprecated method in sun.misc.Unsafe has been called
#     WARNING: sun.misc.Unsafe::objectFieldOffset has been called by scala.runtime.LazyVals$ (.../sbt-launch.jar)
#     WARNING: Please consider reporting this to the maintainers of class scala.runtime.LazyVals$
#     WARNING: sun.misc.Unsafe::objectFieldOffset will be removed in a future release
--sun-misc-unsafe-memory-access=allow

# X509Helper uses the JDK's internal certificate builder, which the JVM keeps behind the module boundary. X509Helper
# belongs to the egress proxy subproject, and the launcher's tests, which issue certificates with it, run in this JVM.
# build.sbt records why the launcher's tests do not fork; the proxy's own suites do
# (ko-agent-egress-proxy/app/build.sbt).
--add-exports=java.base/sun.security.x509=ALL-UNNAMED
--add-exports=java.base/sun.security.util=ALL-UNNAMED
